    [CI] Install triton-ascend from pinned OBS wheel (#19471)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Install triton-ascend from the prebuilt OBS wheel instead of the pip
    index, and move the install into the "Install pinned dependencies"
    section next to the other architecture-selected wheels. The wheel URL is
    resolved inside the existing TARGETPLATFORM case so it reuses
    ARCH_SUFFIX, and the pip uninstall stays in the vllm-ascend install
    step.
    
    Pin TRITON_ASCEND_VERSION to the OBS release directory 20261019175332
    and add TRITON_ASCEND_PACKAGE_VERSION=3.6.0, both overridable via build
    args.
    
    Applies to Dockerfile, Dockerfile.a3, Dockerfile.a5 and their openEuler
    variants. The 310P images do not install triton-ascend.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    ---
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [ ] **Boundary / edge-case coverage**: I reviewed whether this change
    involves
    boundary conditions (e.g. empty input, single/zero element, min/max
    values,
    off-by-one, sequence-length limits, integer overflow). Where applicable,
    I
    added unit tests covering these edge cases in `tests/ut/` or
    `tests/e2e/`.
    - [ ] **Regression test**: If this PR fixes a bug, I added a regression
    test
      that would fail without the fix.
    - [ ] **Error / failure path coverage**: I covered abnormal paths
    (exceptions,
    timeouts, out-of-range, division by zero) in addition to the happy path.
    - [ ] **Meaningful & reliable tests**: New tests assert real behavior
    and are
      not written merely to satisfy CI.
    - [ ] **Performance impact**: If this PR touches a performance-sensitive
    path,
      I attached benchmark results and added performance regression tests.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
